{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/news/funding-boost-for-british-companies-to-supercharge-uk-munitions-production","content_id":"fc888816-443d-40c9-9fba-7d07de8e1070","description":"22 companies, including British SMEs, will receive contracts worth up to £300,000 each to carry out feasibility studies on sites for new UK energetics manufacturing plants.","details":{"attachments":[],"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><ul>\n  <li>22 companies – including British SMEs from England, Scotland, Wales – to receive up to £300,000 each to develop proposals for the creation of new factories producing energetic materials used in munitions.</li>\n  <li>Part of government’s work to rebuild the nation’s homegrown ammunition and energetics manufacturing capability, boosting defence readiness and re-industrialisation of Britain. </li>\n  <li>The substances created will include explosives, propellants and pyrotechnics which are essential components of weapons including small arms, artillery, mortars, countermeasures, bombs and missiles.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>Britain’s homegrown munitions manufacturing industry has been boosted today, with the Ministry of Defence (MOD) placing contracts with 22 companies to fund studies into possible sites for new energetic materials factories.</p>\n\n<p>The contracts, worth up to £300,000 each, will benefit a number of small and medium sized businesses in England, Scotland and Wales.</p>\n\n<p>Energetic materials are the explosives, propellants and pyrotechnics that are essential components of weapons and key to ensuring the UK’s ability to defend itself and deter threats.</p>\n\n<p>The studies will help bring high-skilled manufacturing back to industrial communities across the UK, with work to focus on which sites could be used to build at least six new munitions factories.</p>\n\n<p>The war in Ukraine shows the importance of the fast resupply of munitions by industry, and the studies are advancing the MOD’s work to re-establish a sovereign, ‘always on’ pipeline for munitions supply – boosting warfighting readiness and enhancing the UK’s ability to deter threats while providing skilled manufacturing jobs across the country.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"minister-for-defence-readiness-and-industry-luke-pollard-mp-said\">Minister for Defence Readiness and Industry Luke Pollard MP said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p class=\"last-child\">This Government is building the munitions and energetics factories of the future, restoring Britain’s sovereign manufacturing capabilities after decades of decline and helping us to re-industrialise. By investing across England, Scotland and Wales, we are strengthening our warfighting readiness and security of supply, while creating at least 1,000 high-skilled jobs in the future in communities that have long been the backbone of British industry and will be again.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n<p>Each of the companies selected by the MOD will receive funding of up to £300,000 each to develop detailed proposals to manufacture energetics materials and the appropriate sites which they should be based at.</p>\n\n<p>In November 2025, the Government announced that at least 13 potential sites had been identified across the UK for the manufacture of munitions and explosives, including:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>Monmouthshire </li>\n  <li>Cumbria </li>\n  <li>Dumfries and Galloway  </li>\n  <li>North Ayrshire </li>\n  <li>Shropshire </li>\n  <li>Cheshire </li>\n  <li>Derbyshire </li>\n  <li>Essex </li>\n  <li>Worcestershire </li>\n  <li>Hampshire </li>\n  <li>Pembrokeshire </li>\n  <li>Falkirk</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The studies follow £11.1 billion being allocated through the Defence Investment Plan for munitions and weapons – increasing UK stockpiles and ensuring our Armed Forces have the right ‘high-low’ mix of capabilities to defeat the full range of targets in the most efficient way.</p>\n\n<p>The companies are expected to return their findings by the end of September 2026 with construction of the new energetics munitions factories planned to start by the end of 2026. </p>\n\n<p>On completion of the feasibility studies, the top proposals will be offered Front End Engineering Design (FEED) contracts worth up to £5 million each to develop engineering designs for at least six new munitions and energetics factories.</p>\n\n<h3 id=\"commodore-caroline-dix-mbe-deputy-director-lethality-and-protect-in-national-armaments-director-group--materiel-said\">Commodore Caroline Dix MBE, Deputy Director Lethality and Protect in National Armaments Director Group – Materiel, said:</h3>\n\n<blockquote>\n  <p>National Armaments – Materiel is pleased to announce the award of feasibility study contracts to a diverse cohort of companies, from innovative SMEs to major defence primes and major chemical industry partners. This is a significant step towards rebuilding the UK’s sovereign energetics industry.</p>\n\n  <p>The studies will identify how we can grow UK production of the explosives, propellants and pyrotechnics that underpin military capability, driving investment, innovation and skilled jobs across the country.</p>\n\n  <p class=\"last-child\">Above all, it will help ensure the Armed Forces have a secure and resilient supply of the munitions they need to fight and win.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-29T08:30:04Z"}],"emphasised_organisations":["d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12"],"images":[{"caption":null,"content_type":"image/jpeg","sources":{"s216":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731ae2a1415/s216_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s300":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s465":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f53468995326/s465_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s630":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a983a846/s630_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s712":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46e90e0731a4dcff75/s712_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","s960":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"type":"lead"}],"political":true},"document_type":"press_release","first_published_at":"2026-07-29T09:30:04+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/news/funding-boost-for-british-companies-to-supercharge-uk-munitions-production","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/news/funding-boost-for-british-companies-to-supercharge-uk-munitions-production","base_path":"/government/news/funding-boost-for-british-companies-to-supercharge-uk-munitions-production","content_id":"fc888816-443d-40c9-9fba-7d07de8e1070","document_type":"press_release","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-29T08:30:04Z","schema_name":"news_article","title":"Funding boost for British companies to supercharge UK munitions production","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/funding-boost-for-british-companies-to-supercharge-uk-munitions-production","withdrawn":false}],"emphasised_organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D17","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","base_path":"/government/organisations/ministry-of-defence","content_id":"d994e55c-48c9-4795-b872-58d8ec98af12","details":{"acronym":"MOD","brand":"ministry-of-defence","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d46d3bf7f618eda94d2/s960_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63495d468fa8f5346732690e/s300_ministry-of-defence-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"mod","formatted_title":"Ministry<br/>of Defence"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"lo